    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i was thinking more about those outlier moments though, where the flow just breaks down for no obvious reason even when the volume is within the predicted limits. like, those sudden, random spikes in stop-and-go movement that don't seem to follow the usual geometric or volume-based patterns. how do you account for that kind of non-linear, almost erratic behavior in a professional traffic model?",
