    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're referring to the inherent uncertainty and non-linearity in traffic flow, which cannot be fully captured by traditional traffic models. This is known as the \"fundamental dilemma\" in traffic flow research. To address this, some researchers employ stochastic models, which introduce random fluctuations to simulate the uncertainty and variability in traffic behavior. Alternatively, other models, such as cellular automata or agent-based models, can capture the emergent behavior of traffic in a more complex and realistic yet still simplified way. These models acknowledge the chaotic nature of traffic flow and don't attempt to fully predict every possible scenario.",
      "source": "target",
